  "doc.title": "Why a USB Drive Never Hits Its Label · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "Why does a 7 GB/s NVMe SSD in a USB enclosure measure a few hundred MB/s to two or three GB/s, and what do “Gen 2×2” and “40Gbps” on the box mean? Nine models you can drag: the USB 2.0 microframe, from a name to the line rate, Bulk-Only’s one-at-a-time exchange, UASP’s queue, the bottleneck along the bridge chain, thermal throttling, the PCIe tunnel of Thunderbolt and USB4, and the few dies inside a flash drive.",
